        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>Conjugate the Akan verb <i>\u00abdi\u00bb</i> (to eat) in the <b>perfective aspect</b> for the following subjects:<br>1. Me (I)<br>2. Wo (You singular)<br>3. W\u0254n (They)</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The perfective aspect in Akan is formed by adding the prefix <i>\u00aba-\u00bb</i> to the verb stem. The correct conjugations are:<br>1. <i>\u00abMedi\u00bb</i> (I have eaten)<br>2. <i>\u00abWodi\u00bb</i> (You have eaten)<br>3. <i>\u00abW\u0254adi\u00bb</i> (They have eaten)</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
